  "checked_engineering_obligations": [
    "A strict receipt reread precedes exactly one get_attempt inspection selected by the trusted attempt identifier; invalid expectations and receipt failures do not inspect the registry.",
    "Nested caller expectations are captured before receipt I/O. Canonical finite JSON binds identities without bool/int conflation and rejects coherent substitutions against independently retained commitments.",
    "Independent raw-row and row-hash-list commitments bind the same trusted producer's same ordered 4096-row slice; neither hash is derived from the other.",
    "Success with null or arbitrary JSON callback result, failed-after-counts and unfinalized-after-counts preserve observed lifecycle facts and never grant retry. Missing attempts reject; inspection exceptions propagate.",
    "Inspected lifecycle rows require plain terminal-count fields and four false flags. Count receipt values remain distinct from callback result values."
  ],
